<title>INDONESIA: Mulia says to raise prices of products.</title>
<headline>Mulia says to raise prices of products.</headline>
<dateline>JAKARTA 1996-12-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Indonesian glass and tile manufacturer PT Mulia Industrindo said on Thursday it will raise the domestic prices of its glass products by between 13 and 18 percent from January 1 next year.</p>
<p>Mulia said in a statement its subsidiary, PT Muliaglass, had obtained ISO 9002 certification from SGS Yarsley International Certification Services Limited, United Kingdom last November.</p>
<p>&quot;With the combination of the two factors, we believe our company can achieve a net profit of 180 billion in 1997,&quot; Mulia investor relations director Rony Djohan said in the statement.</p>
<p>-- Jakarta newsroom +6221 384-6364</p>
</text>
